    "durationMs": 185915,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Here's what I built and confirmed:\n\n**Implementation** (`app/`): FastAPI app with SQLAlchemy 2.0-style ORM over psycopg 3 (the `DATABASE_URL` from the env is rewritten to `postgresql+psycopg://` at engine creation — no hard-coded credentials). Pydantic schemas validate `url` as an absolute http/https URL with a host and `code` as 4–20 chars of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`, while storing the URL string unchanged. Redirects do an atomic `UPDATE ... SET clicks = clicks + 1 ... RETURNING url`, and exception handlers turn 404/422 (including malformed JSON) into JSON with an `error` field.\n\n**Persistence**: Alembic migration `0001_create_links.py` creates the `links` table (unique indexed `code`, `clicks` default 0, `created_at`); `sh start.sh` runs `alembic upgrade head` then `exec uvicorn` in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` (cwd-independent). README documents startup; `requirements.txt` pins the preinstalled stack (no extras added).\n\n**Verification** — 60+ automated checks, all passing:\n- 201 with `clicks: 0`, generated and custom codes, URLs echoed byte-for-byte unchanged\n- 409 duplicates, 422 for malformed JSON / bad url / bad code boundaries (3, 21, unicode, spaces)\n- 302 with exact `Location`, clicks incremented exactly once, 404s with error fields, ascending-order listing with correct `total`\n- Server killed and restarted: all links and click counts survived\n- 25 parallel redirects → exactly 25 clicks; 10 parallel duplicate creates → one 201, nine 409\n- Fresh-boot run against an empty database from a different working directory\n\nThe database is left migrated at head with zero rows, and no servers are running."
